As with most mammalian puberty, male adolescence also implies the emergence of maleness in physical signs that are uniquely human. The pubic hair that develops on the chest is usually removed before a boy starts shaving his beard. Similarly, the voice becomes deeper, but remains high. The growth of the penis and of testicular tissue and seminal vesicles usually follow after puberty has been established.
Another social milestone marking the shift for women from childhood and into adulthood comes in the form of the rite of marriage. Even if this custom varies by individual, cultural, and religious group, marriage symbolizes the woman's entry into adulthood.

, Moldavian, Ukrainian, and Latvian SFSR issued a declaration, called the Belavezha Accords. In it, the Russian SFC agreed to a series of concessions to the other republics:
The Russian SFC would:
- renounce the use of force to resolve disputes with any other republic;
- withdraw its troops to its own borders;
- allow only the RF troops into any of the republics;
- recognize the independence of all of the former Soviet republics, except for the Russian Republic, and accept their sovereignty;
- accept all of the provisions of the Union Treaty, except for those relating to the RF presidency.
The declaration was rejected by all of the republic governments.

