Administered by the Justice Department, the Civil Liberties Advisory Committee was tasked with investigating, advising and reporting back to the President on the use and abuse of civil liberties and civil liberties in the United States.
The Civil Liberties Advisory Committee carried out an exhaustive survey of existing state and local institutional restraints on civil liberties over an extended period. The resulting report was entitled Report on Civil Rights Situation in the United States. The report identified no fewer than 11 hundred and forty seven restrictions on civil liberties, including (but not limited to):
